[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Read one report at a time,
the ticket held more than one bug. Engineering closed it on 5 October. The desk merged on subject line alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and the subjects are the same for every
problem below: "wrong day", "dates mixed up". The bodies are not.

<Callout>
Closed 5 October. Parser: fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`). Form hint: won't fix,
the booking-v3 form is retired. One-day move: no fix; reopen its ticket if these reports keep coming.
</Callout>

## The count

The desk's own view of the ticket, built from the export at render time. Reports are placed by
their tenant (locale and booking form, `causes.ts`), not by the intake tag, which is a guess from
the reporter's browser. The one-day reports are counted where the desk files them, under `parser`,
and footnoted below the table.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| problem | ticket | outcome |
|---|---|---|
| `parser`: day and month swap | [ai-training#1](https://github.com/rogasoft/ai-training/issues/1) | fixed 5 Oct · closed |
| `hint`: booking-v3 form tells people to type month first | [ai-training#2](https://github.com/rogasoft/ai-training/issues/2) | won't fix, form retired · closed |
| one-day move: the footnoted reports | [ai-training#3](https://github.com/rogasoft/ai-training/issues/3) | no fix · closed, reopen if it recurs |

## The problems

**`parser`: day and month swap.** The shared parser reads every date month first. All our tenants
on file write the day first, so 7 April becomes 4 July. Where a report in this row names both
dates, they are the same day and month, swapped. This is the bug #4471 was opened for. Fixed on 5 October.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form tells people to type month first.** Tenants on `booking-v3` show
`MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their people type what the hint says, and the form reads the
date the tenant's way, day first. The parser fix does not touch this. Engineering retired the
booking-v3 form instead of fixing the hint. Only reports sent through the form of a `booking-v3` tenant are in
this row; the same tenants' app and email reports are parser reports.

**`one-day`: the date moves by a day, it does not swap.** These reports describe a date that is
one day early or late, a meeting that lands on different days for people in different cities, and
an invite that arrives before the booking was made. No day and month are swapped. This reads as a
time zone or day-boundary bug in how invites are built. The desk notes these reports
(`desk-notes.json`) and counts them under `parser`, where its view footnotes them. The parser fix will not change them.

## What to do on the desk

- Point new reports at the row they match, not at #4471 by subject.
- After the parser fix, a new one-day report is not "#4471 still broken": reopen ai-training#3.
- Matching on subject merged three bugs into one count. Read the body before you merge.

